{
  "manufacturer": "Rishabh Instruments",
  "manufacturer_slug": "rishabh-instruments",
  "model": "RISH ED11XX / EC11XX / ER11XX single-phase DIN-rail energy meters",
  "model_slug": "rish-ed-ec-er11xx",
  "short_model": "EC11XX",
  "aliases": [
    "RISH ED11X1",
    "RISH EC11X1",
    "RISH ER11X1",
    "ED1111",
    "EC1111",
    "ER1111",
    "RISH ED11XX",
    "RISH EC11XX",
    "RISH ER11XX"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Rishabh RISH ED11XX (direct), EC11XX (CT) and ER11XX (RJ12 CT) single-phase DIN-rail meters in their Modbus (x1) versions, per operating manual DMAN-00IM-1071 Rev. M.",
  "summary": "Single-phase DIN-rail energy meters from Rishabh in direct-connected (ED), CT-connected (EC) and RJ12 CT (ER) versions; the Modbus variants have an RS-485 port speaking Modbus RTU. Every measured value is an IEEE 754 float in two registers, readable as input registers from 30001 or as holding registers at the same offset from 40001. This map covers voltage, current, power, PF, frequency, demands, total/tariff/partial energies and the main setup registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Table 4 prints 3X and 4X numbers next to the hex start address (30001 = 00 00, 30071 = 00 46). Wire address = number - 30001 (FC04) or - 40001 (FC03); every row was checked against the printed hex and parameter number. The setup example reads 46007 at 17 76."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Operating Manual RISH ED11XX / EC11XX / ER11XX DIN rail mount Single Phase AC Energy Meter",
    "doc_number": "DMAN-00IM-1071 Rev. M",
    "revision_date": "09/26",
    "url": "https://rishabh.co.in/uploads/product/rish-ed11x1-66/RISH%20ED_EC_ER_11XX_Operating_Manual%20-%20REV_M.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 16-21 (protocol, data format, examples, Table 4), pp. 24-32 (4X examples, Tables 6-8)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The data-format table states IEEE 754 floats, most significant byte first. The voltage example returns 43 66 00 00 (230 V) and the current example 40 A0 00 00 (5 A), so word order is ABCD.",
    "Every 3X value is also a 4X holding register at the same offset (30001 -> 40001); only the 3X copies are listed.",
    "Left out: parameter 42 (printed with the same name as 43), parameter 108 'Partial Active Import Energy' (unit printed as Wh, unlike its kWh siblings), the 'long energy' Table 5 (30513-30655, format not described) and the user-assignable registers (31025-31051).",
    "Units are as printed (Volts -> V, Amp -> A). Energy overflow counts increase each time the matching energy passes 99999.999.",
    "Up to 40 parameters per read request.",
    "Table 4 prints 'Total Apparent Energy' (and its overflow count) twice in each block: at 30123/30125 and again at 30139/30141 (same for T1 30159/30161 vs 30175/30177, T2 30195/30197 vs 30211/30213, partial 30231/30233 vs 30247/30249). The first copy of each pair is left out because its real meaning is unclear; the second copy sits where the long-energy Table 5 puts total apparent energy.",
    "Default stop bits are not settled: the front-panel section gives nonE1 (no parity, 1 stop) but Table 6 prints Comsetup default 9 (9600, no parity, 2 stop). Both agree on 9600 baud and no parity. Some setup rows also differ between ED and EC/ER models; only the clearly described rows are listed."
  ],
